{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm","id":769221,"title":"Lack of Swimming Charm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-19T07:24:33-08:00","id":769221,"title":"Lack of Swimming Charm","content":"So, this is something that has bothered me quite a bit. Especially since pretty much every GM I've ever had has been like &quot;Yeah, I'd let your movement speed affecting charms help with swimming... if there were swimming charms.&quot; The lack seems strange since it's not like there's going to be any direction other than South where it'll be near useless. The West is going to favor it, but North and East are going to have a lot of use for it as well (note the huge rivers in the East). The Blessed Isle of course has similar use.<br /> <br /> So... other than the past editions of Exalted ignoring it, why don't we have any in the core? And that said, does anyone have any good ideas/charms to fill the gap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:31:32-08:00","id":769226,"title":"","content":"I'd probably just let running Charms apply when swimming since swimming-specific Charms seem pretty niche for no actual value to making them super specific to swimming. While the actual movements are different the general principles are the same if we're talking about racing, endurance for going for awhile, etc. <br /> <br /> Hell, I'd let jumping charms apply when &quot;breaching,&quot; because why not?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:42:42-08:00","id":769231,"title":"","content":"As I said, I've not had any GMs who were that permissive, and based on the design of the charms, it seems like they didn't intend for those to aid in swimming (Though, if I'm wrong, I welcome being told the intent was meant to be more general).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:05:47-08:00","id":769256,"title":"","content":"As they're Athletics charms, and Athletics covers swimming, I'd let them apply. I mean, I think you are right in the sense that their fluff is all about running. I guess the writers just didn't feel the need for something so niche?<br /> (It seems weird to say swimming is niche... but thinking about it, I don't think I've ever seen it come up in games. Even our western games. The only people who ever swam seemed to be Water-Aspects who were awesome at it anyway)<br /> <br /> If your ST disagrees, and it comes up enough that you want swimming charms, maybe suggest a custom Athletics charm that lets you apply Athletics-movement charms to swimming?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:13:27-08:00","id":769265,"title":"","content":"I mean a lot of the Athletics charms are pretty nonspecific about what a test of speed is and I can't help but think that's deliberate. Winning stride discipline, onrush burst method, one extra step and triumph forged God body could all RaW apply to swimming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:25:09-08:00","id":769274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769256#post769256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even our western games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were you out to sea a lot? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:43:55-08:00","id":769282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769231#post769231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, I've not had any GMs who were that permissive</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly that sounds like an ST problem not a rules problem. <br /> <br /> Surely the design intent is not that Exalted athletes can be great at running, jumping, weight-lifting, and gymnastics, but somehow suck at swimming with no way to improve it. <br /> <br /> There's not a need for Charms which apply only to swimming. The value in Solar Charms being so niche is extremely low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769256#post769256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If your ST disagrees, and it comes up enough that you want swimming charms, maybe suggest a custom Athletics charm that lets you apply Athletics-movement charms to swimming?</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a bad idea but I really hate air-breathing mermaid design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:44:51-08:00","id":769284,"title":"","content":"Let's never forget the lessons Deus Ex taught us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:46:08-08:00","id":769285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769274#post769274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were you out to sea a lot? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in my Western game, only one PC routinely gets into the water, and he has a hearthstone that gives him enhanced underwater mobility and the ability to breathe water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:46:08-08:00","id":769286,"title":"","content":"Would holding your breath be Resistance, Integrity, or Athletics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:46:27-08:00","id":769287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769282#post769282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly that sounds like an ST problem not a rules problem.<br /> <br /> Surely the design intent is not that Exalted athletes can be great at running, jumping, weight-lifting, and gymnastics, but somehow suck at swimming with no way to improve it.<br /> <br /> There's not a need for Charms which apply only to swimming. The value in Solar Charms being so niche is extremely low.<br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't a bad idea but I really hate air-breathing mermaid design.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we have a charm in the book which is specifically to kill a very limited subset of sociopaths with a letter. I'm not sure the writers agree on that point with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:49:23-08:00","id":769289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769286#post769286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would holding your breath be Resistance, Integrity, or Athletics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably Stamina+Resistance. Not sure how Integrity would ever apply. Unless it was 2e kitchen sink Integrity and flaring your anima counts as having infinite breath in your lungs, refreshes you like a full night of sleep, and instantly fills your stomach and rehydrated you. <br /> <br /> I think the &quot;explore the oceans on one held breath&quot; Charm is in Sail though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769287#post769287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we have a charm in the book which is specifically to kill a very limited subset of sociopaths with a letter. I'm not sure the writers agree on that point with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note how many people have serious reservations about that Charm. And it's one of a few exceptions when you take the Solar Charmset as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:50:43-08:00","id":769290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769286#post769286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would holding your breath be Resistance, Integrity, or Athletics?</div> </div> </div> </div>As per Strong Lungs, it's Athletics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:54:22-08:00","id":769293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769289#post769289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note how many people have serious reservations about that Charm. And it's one of a few exceptions when you take the Solar Charmset as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>As do I, but my point it, writer intent for how flexible things are seems to be all over the board in places. And it's not like that's the only charm with a weird level of niche when compared to others. Which is sorta the problem. Sure, we can say we think they intend flexibility or don't... but I am not a mind reader, so I don't actually know their intent, and I'm not willing to assume it based on the data we have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:06:31-08:00","id":769310,"title":"","content":"As the most recent ST in question, my position is a bit more nuanced than provided,--<br /> <br /> --if the charm is a generic movement charm, like a lot of the Athletics charms are, those are fine and work with whatever. By which means, charms that enhance a rush or have some effect related to combat movement or what not. Those are cool! But, some of the charms are pretty strictly focused on <i>running</i> and it wouldn't make sense to apply them to swimming as well. It's not like I think swimming-related charms were left out of the book on purpose, and there's plenty of room for charm-tech in that specific category if you want it...<br /> <br /> ...I mean, lightning speed and racing hare method are generic. Feather Foot Style or Spider Foot Style, though, don't really translate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:09:13-08:00","id":769312,"title":"","content":"To clarify my prior point; historically, most sailors have been unable to swim, because if you fall into the water from a moving ship that is at sea, being unable to swim will not save you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:21:57-08:00","id":769327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769312#post769312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify my prior point; historically, most sailors have been unable to swim, because if you fall into the water from a moving ship that is at sea, being unable to swim will not save you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you meant &quot;able,&quot; but yeah, the rest of the PCs in my game are sane enough to not go jumping into the sea all willy-nilly, even the ones that <i>can</i> swim.<br /> <br /> (With the exception of Hectorae, of course, who ended up too burdened by his heavy armor to swim when his lifeboat sank.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:47:00-08:00","id":769346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769284#post769284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's never forget the lessons Deus Ex taught us.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly! That lesson being that you should never EVER put points in swimming when poison resistance is an option!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:35:13-08:00","id":769387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm#post769221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">other than the past editions of Exalted ignoring it</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a swimming Charm, Swift Water Prana, in <i>Caste Book: Night</i>. Adorjan and Kimbery both had 2e Charms that helped swimming, and 2e Alchemicals had Fluidic Impeller Drive. I think that's it for published Charms.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Past editions didn't <i>ignore</i> swimming, but it definitely wasn't A Big Thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T13:28:55-08:00","id":769498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769310#post769310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the most recent ST in question, my position is a bit more nuanced than provided,--<br /> <br /> --if the charm is a generic movement charm, like a lot of the Athletics charms are, those are fine and work with whatever. By which means, charms that enhance a rush or have some effect related to combat movement or what not. Those are cool! But, some of the charms are pretty strictly focused on <i>running</i> and it wouldn't make sense to apply them to swimming as well. It's not like I think swimming-related charms were left out of the book on purpose, and there's plenty of room for charm-tech in that specific category if you want it...<br /> <br /> ...I mean, lightning speed and racing hare method are generic. Feather Foot Style or Spider Foot Style, though, don't really translate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I meant, though I admit I didn't articulate it very well. Clearly if applying the Charm to swimming makes no logical sense (e.g. Spider Foot Style) then it shouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T15:56:30-08:00","id":769605,"title":"","content":"Note, this wasn't how I understood it, and if this is the case, I've got no issues (especially since the two charms mentioned were the ones I have and wanted to use). Seems it was just a misunderstanding and all you good people helped bring about a resolution. Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T16:47:36-08:00","id":769630,"title":"","content":"Why would movement enhancing charms not apply to swimming...which is movement? Few even mention a type a movement in the <i>fluff, </i>let alone the mechanics. Something which seems rather deliberate. The obvious exceptions being the charms that enhance leaps or allow flight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769293#post769293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As do I, but my point it, writer intent for how flexible things are seems to be all over the board in places. And it's not like that's the only charm with a weird level of niche when compared to others. Which is sorta the problem. Sure, we can say we think they intend flexibility or don't... but I am not a mind reader, so I don't actually know their intent, and I'm not willing to assume it based on the data we have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the rest of the charm set, flexibility is plainly a clear focus over niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 11-19-2015, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T21:32:21-08:00","id":769757,"title":"","content":"Folks.<br /> <br /> A human being that can run at ~31 meters per second can run fast enough to run across the surface of water without sinking (<a href=\"http://sploid.gizmodo.com/how-fast-do-you-have-to-run-if-you-want-to-walk-on-wate-1599455890\" target=\"_blank\">see one source here</a>).<br /> <br /> Why are you swimming when you can Speedy Gonzalez your way to Wu Jian in the time it takes Sabriye to eat a pork bun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T02:06:50-08:00","id":769822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769757#post769757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you swimming when you can Speedy Gonzalez your way to Wu Jian in the time it takes Sabriye to eat a pork bun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because sometimes you want to <i>dive</i> for sunken treasure and other things. maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769312#post769312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify my prior point; historically, most sailors have been unable to swim, because if you fall into the water from a moving ship that is at sea, being unable to swim will not save you.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;historically&quot; and &quot;most sailors&quot; you mean &quot;circa 19th century European&quot;. This is more an issue with their ship design as most other sailors with less awkward-to-climb-back-onto vessels felt swimming was a rather useful skill to master. <br /> <br /> For instance, Polynesians plying the Pacific in outrigger canoes were quite deft swimmers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 11-20-2015, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T15:55:27-08:00","id":770349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769822#post769822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because sometimes you want to <i>dive</i> for sunken treasure and other things. maybe?<br /> <br /> <br /> By &quot;historically&quot; and &quot;most sailors&quot; you mean &quot;circa 19th century European&quot;. This is more an issue with their ship design as most other sailors with less awkward-to-climb-back-onto vessels felt swimming was a rather useful skill to master.<br /> <br /> For instance, Polynesians plying the Pacific in outrigger canoes were quite deft swimmers.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are in the middle of the ocean and in the water, nine times out of ten, it is because there is a storm and you are already dead. Making being able to swim well a moot point. Also, when people say &quot;sailor&quot; they are typically not referring to coastal fisherman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T20:09:17-08:00","id":770476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769757#post769757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Folks.<br /> <br /> A human being that can run at ~31 meters per second can run fast enough to run across the surface of water without sinking (<a href=\"http://sploid.gizmodo.com/how-fast-do-you-have-to-run-if-you-want-to-walk-on-wate-1599455890\" target=\"_blank\">see one source here</a>).<br /> <br /> Why are you swimming when you can Speedy Gonzalez your way to Wu Jian in the time it takes Sabriye to eat a pork bun?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because it's fairly obvious and as was mentioned, you'd stay over the water, which means anything under the water is A) probably harder to notice B) going to be more difficult to reach without swimming (though I suppose there might be some ways around that... still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T14:33:19-07:00","id":1401392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769285#post769285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, in my Western game, only one PC routinely gets into the water, and he has a hearthstone that gives him enhanced underwater mobility and the ability to breathe water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to revive an old thread, but TheCountAlucard would you mind sharing the name/write up for that hearthstone? I'm currently looking for something exactly like that for a game I'm running but haven't had much luck finding something.<br /> <br /> TIA<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25150-siegward-of-catarina","name":"Siegward of Catarina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T15:10:26-07:00","id":1401397,"title":"","content":"Not sure about breathing water but the Stone of Aquatic Prowess on page 134 of Arms of the Chosen lets you hold your breath for hours and ignore cold and pressure once you get to the second evocation. The first gives you +2 non-charm to all movement actions underwater, extends holding your breath to minutes and adds the buoyant tag to armor it's socketed to. Don't know if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T15:18:18-07:00","id":1401399,"title":"","content":"Stone of Aquatic Prowess (Water, Standard)<br /> Keywords: None<br /> This slick, colorless gem so resembles water that it\u2019s<br /> invisible when immersed. When mounted in an attuned<br /> hearthstone socket, the stone offers the opportunity to<br /> awaken the following Evocations:<br /> Aquatic Adventurer\u2019s Spirit<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Like an otter, the Exalt is as comfortable in water as<br /> on land. She adds two non-Charm dice to aquatic<br /> movement actions, and measures how long she can<br /> hold her breath in minutes instead of rounds. Armor<br /> socketed with the hearthstone gains the Buoyant<br /> tag.<br /> Benthic Depths Adaptation<br /> Cost: \u2014(3m, 1i); Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Aquatic Adventurer\u2019s Spirit<br /> The Exalt calls the ocean\u2019s floor home. She measures<br /> how long she can hold her breath in hours instead<br /> of rounds, and neither the cold nor pressure of the<br /> deep can harm or impede her. Furthermore, whenever<br /> she successfully dodges an attack underwater,<br /> she may spend three motes, one Initiative to move a<br /> single range band downward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T15:55:36-07:00","id":1401409,"title":"","content":"We had a 1e charm that did this. Allow me to convert it.<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fish Swimming Technique</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost</b>\u200b</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 3m\u037e </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u200b: Athletics 2 Essence 1\u037e </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:\u200b Reflexive</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u200b</b>: None</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u200b</b>: One day</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite charms</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u200b: None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Solar swims as well at those who call the ocean home. Upon activating this charm the Solar becomes able to swim in the water as well as he can move on land, suffering no penalties to moving in water. He may move or down a range brand underwater as a single action, including leaping one range brand out of the water to surprise the Solar\u2019s foes. The Solar also reduces the difficulty of all swimming checks by 1, minimum 0. Lastly any speed enhancement charms that would function on land function just as well in the water itself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Essence 4, the cost of this charm is reduced to 0m.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T18:29:55-07:00","id":1401415,"title":"","content":"Yeah, exactly that IMO. Although I'd also amend it so that while the Charm is actice any Charms that would fascilitate movement on land could do the same for water.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm now thinking of artifacts fow use in or on water. What kind would be good for that and what should some evocation effects be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T22:52:15-07:00","id":1401433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=1401415#post1401415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I'd also amend it so that while the Charm is actice any Charms that would fascilitate movement on land could do the same for water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. Last sentence of the charm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T23:15:25-07:00","id":1401436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=1401415#post1401415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, exactly that IMO. Although I'd also amend it so that while the Charm is actice any Charms that would fascilitate movement on land could do the same for water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do any of the Solar movement Charms specify they only facilitate movement on land in the first place? I'm only checking Athletics at the moment, but the only ones I see that even <i>mention</i> the ground are Thunderbolt Attack Prana (where whether <i>the opponent</i> is grounded or aerial affects the range of the attack), Eagle Wing Method (which uses the ground to take off)... hold on...<br /> <br /> \u200bOkay, I found <i>one</i>. Hurricane Spirit Speed.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill seems a tad unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T00:33:27-07:00","id":1401442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Siegward of Catarina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=1401392#post1401392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to revive an old thread, but TheCountAlucard would you mind sharing the name/write up for that hearthstone? I'm currently looking for something exactly like that for a game I'm running but haven't had much luck finding something.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were using the 2e version of the Stone of Aquatic Prowess because Arms of the Chosen had not been published yet.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, once it was, we switched to using that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T02:23:51-07:00","id":1401448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=1401415#post1401415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm now thinking of artifacts fow use in or on water. What kind would be good for that and what should some evocation effects be?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Folding Ship! Folding Ship! Folding Ship!</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Ahem, sorry about that. As a starter for 10:<br /> <br /> Conquering Tide might be a decent reference point for vessels with actual evocations \u2013 a black jade man-o-war with evocations designed to boost pursuit at sea (so sailing speed bonuses, penalties on opponents stratagems, boosts to sail and investigation charms). It's like the world's greatest coastguard cutter.<br /> <br /> Different craft could maybe do different things, a spec-ops style submersible that enhances your stealth charms for commando-style raids or smuggling for example.<br /> <br /> On a more personal scale, maybe DBs as inspiration: a bow offering an evocation along the lines of Fang-Of-The-Depths Draw (shooting underwater for no penalty) or scale-mail that apes Dragon Surmounts The Waterfall or the like maybes.<br /> <br /> (One day I <i>will </i>get to play a Water-aspect who has those charms along with Thousand Thorn Artillery and spend all game coming up with excuses why a human-scale hunter-killer submarine is the perfect solution to whatever problem we are currently facing...)<br /> <br /> Would think an aquatic version of a Clockwork Bird would be useful \u2013 something able to dive underwater with you, explore small crevices and offer light and comms where needed, basically an Exalted UUV.<br /> <br /> Maybe a harpoon with bonuses for attacking large aquatic beasts or penetrating hulls etc.<br /> <br /> Some way of communicating with the surface and/or over long distance would probably be handy too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 07-07-2020, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T04:00:20-07:00","id":1401455,"title":"","content":"I did mean like personal sized items, not a full vehicle which folding ship is.<br /> <br /> I remembered after I posted, a long time ago, maybe 1E, I had an idea for a shield that could be ridden like a surfboard while on water. The purpose was for storming beaches, you'd ride it ashore from youir ships then pick it up and carry it for defense when you reach land. Is that too silly an idea, or would that work (with a few other tricks too of course)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T07:33:08-07:00","id":1401479,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want a personal-scale item, there's always the black jade crossbow in <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> that pulls you along behind it like an aquatic Thor, so your shield doesn't sound outlandish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:26:27-07:00","id":1401766,"title":"","content":"Swimming is not a special movement mode that demands its own subsystem.<br /> Just like climbing isn't. They basically are harder to tread.<br /> <br /> You still move using movement actions, which are reflexive and rarely demand rolls, which remain athletics rolls.<br /> The combat actions for movement are the same, rush and disengage. <br /> <br /> <br /> Read the solar athletics racing/rushing charms. Many at are fluffed at &quot;racing&quot; and &quot;leaping&quot;. A couple mention land in the fluff.<br /> Without exception, they affirm they enhance rushes, with no restriction. Lightning speed mentions &quot;tests of speed of other sorts&quot;.<br /> <br /> This sets precedent in favor of they all simply working for swimming.<br /> It makes sense in-character, as exalts tend to be very broadly competent.<br /> It makes sense reading the mechanics as expansive rather than restricted.<br /> It makes sense from the perspective that swimming's challenges aren't diverse enough to warrant spending more xp on it if you aren't dramatically altering the rules (like feather foot style and its upgrades).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":".  So many typos 07-08-2020, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:44:07-07:00","id":1401773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/769221-lack-of-swimming-charm?p=769290#post769290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per Strong Lungs, it's Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default for holding breath is stamina, and it's not a test.<br /> The merit adds athletics to your stamina. Read it in the rules for deprivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:08:10-07:00","id":1401796,"title":"","content":"Not sure if it's been stated already, but mechanically swimming is still done using Move and Dash actions. There is no &quot;swim&quot; action, so anything that increases your &quot;movement&quot; should increase your swim speed, as well as your climbing speed. The only mechanical difference is that you move at half speed while swimming and climbing, and of course if you are swimming for extended periods you might have to make rolls to hold your breath. I have personally also been okay with effects that &quot;remove all penalty to movement&quot; negating this half speed rule, though that obviously will be a ST preference thing.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think you've just had some really bad luck with your GM rulings. I'd suggest asking them where the &quot;swim&quot; action is listed, and if they can't find it then seriously inquire as to why Charms that improve your Move and Dash actions shouldn't also improve your swim speeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:26:18-07:00","id":1401802,"title":"","content":"Swimming and climbing don't come up very often, but tend to be cornerstones of the given scene. I roll with &quot;generally controlling your movement on water requires a roll that will last you the scene. As normal per any movement, if the waters become dangerous or hard to cross the difficulty of the roll to stay in control is added to whatever traversal rolls being made by the involved parties&quot;.<br /> <br /> In my games most characters that cared for it managed what they wanted just from their normal rolls and enhancers (creatures that had clear advantages over them weren't worth pursuing on their own, so they used different means for the party to reach them like godly aid and devices), so not even the athletics supernal felt a want for swimming charms when presented with the obstacle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you want swimming charms you can make things like &quot;ignore [a lot of] penalties and difficulties to swimming&quot;, &quot;even unconscious you can stay afloat properly to not drown&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T15:48:53-07:00","id":1401981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert E. Howard, \u201cThe Pool of the Black One\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She sat up, her gaze fixed on the rail, over which, to her amazement, a dripping figure clambered. Her dark eyes opened wide, her red lips parted in an O of surprise. The intruder was a stranger to her. Water ran in rivulets from his great shoulders and down his heavy arms. His single garment\u2014a pair of bright crimson silk breeks \u2013 was soaking wet, as was his broad gold-buckled girdle and the sheathed sword it supported. As he stood at the rail, the rising sun etched him like a great bronze statue. He ran his fingers through his streaming black mane, and his blue eyes lit as they rested on the girl.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who are you?&quot; she demanded. &quot;Whence did you come?&quot;<br /> <br /> He made a gesture toward the sea that took in a whole quarter of the compass, while his eyes did not leave her supple figure.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you a merman, that you rise up out of the sea?&quot; she asked, confused by the candor of his gaze, though she was accustomed to admiration.<br /> <br /> Before he could reply, a quick step sounded on the boards, and the master of the carack was glaring at the stranger, fingers twitching at sword-hilt.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who the devil are you, sirrah?&quot; this one demanded in no friendly tone.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am Conan,&quot; the other answered imperturbably. Sancha pricked up her ears anew; she had never heard Zingaran spoken with such an accent as the stranger spoke it.<br /> <br /> &quot;And how did you get aboard my ship?&quot; The voice grated with suspicion.<br /> <br /> &quot;I swam.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Swam!&quot; exclaimed the master angrily. &quot;Dog, would you jest with me? We are far beyond sight of land. Whence do you come?&quot;<br /> <br /> Conan pointed with a muscular brown arm toward the east, banded in dazzling gold by the lifting sun.<br /> <br /> &quot;I came from the Islands.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh!&quot; The other regarded him with increased interest. Black brows drew down over scowling eyes, and the thin lip lifted unpleasantly.<br /> <br /> &quot;So you are one of those dogs of the Barachans.&quot;<br /> <br /> A faint smile touched Conan's lips.<br /> <br /> &quot;And do you know who I am?&quot; his questioner demanded.<br /> <br /> &quot;This ship is the <i>Wastrel</i>; so you must be Zaporavo.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Aye!&quot; It touched the captain's grim vanity that the man should know him. He was a tall man, tall as Conan, though of leaner build. Framed in his steel morion his face was dark, saturnine and hawk-like, wherefore men called him the Hawk. His armor and garments were rich and ornate, after the fashion of a Zingaran grandee. His hand was never far from his sword-hilt.<br /> <br /> There was little favor in the gaze he bent on Conan. Little love was lost between Zingaran renegades and the outlaws who infested the Baracha Islands off the southern coast of Zingara. These men were mostly sailors from Argos, with a sprinkling of other nationalities. They raided the shipping, and harried the Zingaran coast towns, just as the Zingaran buccaneers did, but these dignified their profession by calling themselves Freebooters, while they dubbed the Barachans pirates. They were neither the first nor the last to gild the name of thief.<br /> <br /> Some of these thoughts passed through Zaporavo's mind as he toyed with his sword-hilt and scowled at his uninvited guest. Conan gave no hint of what his own thoughts might be. He stood with folded arms as placidly as if upon his own deck; his lips smiled and his eyes were untroubled.<br /> <br /> &quot;What are you doing here?&quot; the Freebooter demanded abruptly.<br /> <br /> &quot;I found it necessary to leave the rendezvous at Tortage before moonrise last night,&quot; answered Conan. &quot;I departed in a leaky boat, and rowed and bailed all night. Just at dawn I saw your topsails, and left the miserable tub to sink, while I made better speed in the water.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There are sharks in these waters,&quot; growled Zaporavo, and was vaguely irritated by the answering shrug of the mighty shoulders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conan\u2019s no doubt got Athletics Charms, but I don\u2019t think he necessarily needs any <i>specific</i> to swimming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}